[size=5][b]The Cinderworks: The Broken Water Return[/b][/size]

Hi everyone! Here is a look at how Floor One has developed, from early layout experiments into an enclosed industrial complex with its own furniture, machinery and architectural families. The images are development studies and live test captures; the final art direction is still under review.

[i]Prepared native render — The enclosed interior candidate: a prepared overview of the complete floor.[/i]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/83e1b40d52b34bcbe50b5d9662f5a61a37bb2282/images/tower-map/01-whole-floor.png[/img]

[b]Finding the shape of the floor[/b]

The earlier playable map established the preparation and guardian routes. We then explored a sanctuary-led layout, a waterway and exploration layout, and a more direct foundry progression. All three remain concept studies; none was approved for production.

[i]Live native gameplay — The earlier playable Cinderworks, before the original enclosed interior.[/i]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/83e1b40d52b34bcbe50b5d9662f5a61a37bb2282/images/tower-map/02-early-live-floor.png[/img]

[i]Prepared native render — Layout A: an early offline composition study, retained as a concept rather than an approved map.[/i]
