[b]From open courts to a connected interior[/b]

The direction moved toward an enclosed shell: connected rooms, supported thresholds and a water return through the middle. The concept illustration below is a visual target, followed by actual native-rendered geometry.

[i]Prepared native render — The enclosed foundation before the fitted paving and furnishing pass; same prepared camera as the opening overview.[/i]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/83e1b40d52b34bcbe50b5d9662f5a61a37bb2282/images/tower-map/05-enclosed-foundation.png[/img]

[i]AI concept illustration — AI-generated concept illustration used as an art-direction target. This is not implemented geometry.[/i]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/83e1b40d52b34bcbe50b5d9662f5a61a37bb2282/images/tower-map/06-art-direction.png[/img]

[i]Prepared native render — Prepared overhead of the interior candidate: the bridge and service rooms connect the two sides.[/i]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/83e1b40d52b34bcbe50b5d9662f5a61a37bb2282/images/tower-map/07-floor-plan.png[/img]

[b]Giving each working space a purpose[/b]

These matched prepared workshop views show the furnishing and paving pass. The later layout replaces the old rail arrangement with fixed lifting equipment, sorting surfaces, manual trays and a trackless handcart.

[i]Prepared native render — Workshop before: the protected foundation.[/i]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/83e1b40d52b34bcbe50b5d9662f5a61a37bb2282/images/tower-map/08-workshop-before.png[/img]

[i]Prepared native render — Workshop after: fitted slate, machine pads and manual workstations; the old rails are removed.[/i]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/83e1b40d52b34bcbe50b5d9662f5a61a37bb2282/images/tower-map/09-workshop-after.png[/img]

The room tour below uses actual live native-client captures. Different stone, brick and refractory floor treatments help separate refuge, resource preparation, water management and the encounter chambers.

